ains why the output stopped at a width of 5 in train 1; the grid limited it. I'm now verifying the color alternating pattern.\n\n\n**Calculating the Cell Color**\n\nI've determined a clear formula for cell coloring! The key is the distance from the central column. If the distance is even, it's a 7; odd, it's an 8. I've tested this thoroughly against both train examples, and it holds perfectly. I'm now applying this logic to the test input.\n\n\n\n",
